.Dd September 28, 2026
.Dt SW_VERS 1
.Os Darwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm sw_vers
.Nd print system version information
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n | Fl v | Fl e | Fl b | Fl i | Fl x | Fl r
.Nm
.Op Fl P Ar plist
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the product name, product version and build version of the running
system, one per line.
.Pp
Given a single option, only the requested field is printed, without a label.
.Pp
The values come from the supplemental system version dictionary maintained by
CoreFoundation.
With
.Fl P ,
they are instead read from the property list at
.Ar plist ,
which is useful for inspecting a system version file other than the one
currently installed..Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n , Fl -productName
Print the product name, for example
.Dq macOS .
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -ProductName
and
.Fl -productname .
.It Fl v , Fl -productVersion
Print the product version, for example
.Dq 26.5.2 .
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -ProductVersion
and
.Fl -productversion .
.It Fl e , Fl -productVersionExtra
Print the product version extra, the suffix that distinguishes one release
from another within the same product version.
Nothing is printed if the system does not record one.
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -ProductVersionExtra
and
.Fl -productversionextra .
.It Fl b , Fl -buildVersion
Print the build version, for example
.Dq 25F84 .
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -BuildVersion
and
.Fl -buildversion .
.It Fl i , Fl -buildID
Print the build identifier, a unique identifier for the installed system.
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -BuildID
and
.Fl -buildid .
.It Fl x , Fl -XBSVersion
Print the Xcode build version.
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -xbsversion .
This field is no longer recorded by current systems, so nothing is printed.
.It Fl r , Fl -releaseType
Print the release type, for example
.Dq Beta .
The long option is also accepted as
.Fl -ReleaseType
and
.Fl -releasetype .
.It Fl P Ar plist , Fl -plist Ar plist
Read the version information from the property list at
.Ar plist
instead of from the running system.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage message and exit.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
It exits with status 0 on success.
.Pp
It exits with status 1 if an option is unrecognized or missing its argument,
if the system version information cannot be loaded, or if the property list
named by
.Fl P
cannot be read.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Show the full version report:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sw_vers
.Ed
.Pp
Print just the build version:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sw_vers -buildVersion
.Ed
.Pp
Read a system version plist that is not the installed one:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sw_vers -plist /path/to/SystemVersion.plist
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
An error is reported on the standard error output if the system version
information is missing or malformed, or if
.Fl P
names a file that cannot be read as a property list.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr plutil 1
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
command first appeared in NeXTSTEP.
.Pp
The
.Fl e ,
.Fl i ,
.Fl r
and
.Fl x
options, the
.Fl P
option, and the capitalised and all-lowercase spellings of the long
options appeared in Mac OS X 10.13.
